      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. 17-1307"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Daniel L. Geyser",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Non-judicial foreclosures are covered under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act as a direct or indirect attempt to collect a consumer's debt. It is a direct attempt because pre-foreclosure notices are indistinguishable from traditional dunning letters. It is an indirect attempt because the foreclosure process is designed by law to automatically sell the consumer's house to obtain payment on the consumer's debt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Daniel L. Geyser",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They state that there is a default on the debt. They state the amount of the debt owed. They state to whom the debt is owed. And, critically, they state the consequence of failing to satisfy that debt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Geyser, can -- I -- I may be missing something here, so I -- I'd appreciate your help."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So what is the difference between that situation and the non-judicial foreclosure situation where the -- the homeowner is simply notified that the -- the house that -- the mortgage is being foreclosed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At that point, the -- the debtor still owes 100 percent of the same debt they owed before the repossession."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I have another question about your repo man example. You say we need that last sentence to capture him in a(6). But why wouldn't he be captured by the first sentence in a(6) too? Why isn't a repo man a classic debt collector under any definition, even the broad, the very broad ones you proffer for a(6), first sentence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You are arguing, I think, that even if I disagree with you, we disagree with you on the first sentence, you win because of the third sentence, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jonathan C. Bond",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JONATHAN C. BOND FOR THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENT MR. BOND: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In the FDCPA, Congress made a considered compromise judgment between security interest enforcers as debt collectors for a single subsection of the Act, and not for the remainder, including the provisions at issue here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can I ask you one question on what you mean? Imagine we have a person just like this one, he's trying to enforce a securities interest and he doesn't ask for any deficiency payment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, in other words, you're saying if the state were exactly the same, but it just didn't say anything about newspapers, then his client would win?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: What -- what -- what"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Can I see if I under -- I'm sorry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1307",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Is your answer that we determine that by reference to state law and what is mandated in order to collect on a security interest or to enforce a security interest?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
